  "term": "cerebellar ataxia",
  "definition": "Cerebellar ataxia is a loss of coordination in voluntary movement caused by disease of the cerebellum. It commonly involves inaccurate reaching, shaking during attempted movement, difficulty with rapid alternating movements, and an unsteady gait.",
